
# Fuxing Wang, June 2019

0. How to start

a. Convert HCLIM fa outputs to nc format 
   run the script under fa2nc (height file, constant variable)
   and under fa2nc_multi_file (atmospheric variable files)

   For aladin 12km simulation, not all the variables have hourly values.
   husL65, uamL65, vamL65 only have 3 hourly values.
   We then use 3 hourly values for all the variables. 
   Select 3-hourly values from 1-hourly values & 
   add the record 1 August 00:00 after the time 31 July 21:00. 
   using script: fa2nc_multi_file/sel_value.sh

b. Regrid of HCLIM output 
   The SURFEX grid depends on the forcing data.
   If someone wants to have a different grid/resolution with the corresponding HCLIM output, a spatial interpolation is required
   Run Regrid/regrid.sh to interpolate the model grids from low resolution to high resolution (e.g., 3000m --> 500m)

c. Run prepare_HCLIM_file.sh to integrate all variables into a 2D netcdf file
   If SCA_VARY, change the value of the 1st record 
   INTEGRAL_OF_SURFACE_DOWNWELLING_SHORTWAVE_FLUX_IN_AIR_WRT_TIME, and
   SCATTERED_SHORT_WAVE_RADIATION, to zero using the script: 
   fa2nc_multi_file/change_var_value.sh

d. Run run.sh for create_forcing

e. If forcing time step is not 1H (e.g., 3H), 
 - change in config.yml* file from instant=3600 to instant=10800 before run run.sh
 - after run.sh, run change_time_ncname.sh to correct FRC_TIME_STP in forcing netcdf file (in folder SURFEX_FORC) from 3600 to 10800. 

f. Initial condition for PREP
   If needed, run /home/sm_fuxwa/Script/lfi2fa.sh to get initial condition file in lfi format for PREP/SURFEX

Notes:
--- MetCoOP, Svalbard, MUMS, MUMS_TEST, ... are the different experiments
--- some scripts (prepare_HCLIM_file.sh, run.sh, ...) are under the experiment.
--- The scripts change_fname.sh, change_var_value.sh under fa2nc_multi_file, and change_nc_name.sh under MUMS might also needed.

1. pattern file got from:
http://thredds.met.no/thredds/catalog/aromearcticarchive/2015/10/21/catalog.html

2. The SURFEX offline forcing variables vs HCLIM38 output variables:
ZS
	ZS:long_name = "Surface_Orography" ;
ZREF
	ZREF:long_name = "Reference_Height" ;
	ZREF:units = "m" ;
UREF, 
	UREF:long_name = "Reference_Height_for_Wind" ;
	UREF:units = "m" ;
Tair, tas_fp
	Tair:long_name = "Near_Surface_Air_Temperature" ;
	Tair:units = "K" ;
	Tair:measurement_height = "30m" ;
Qair, huss_fp
	Qair:long_name = "Near_Surface_Specific_Humidity" ;
	Qair:units = "Kg/Kg" ;
	Qair:measurement_height = "30m" ;
Wind, uas_fp vas_fp
	Wind:long_name = "Wind_Speed" ;
	Wind:units = "m/s" ;
	Wind:measurement_height = "30m" ;
DIR_SWdown, rsdsdir
	DIR_SWdown:long_name = "Surface_Indicent_Direct_Shortwave_Radiation" ;
	DIR_SWdown:units = "W/m2" ;
SCA_SWdown, 
	SCA_SWdown:long_name = "Surface_Incident_Diffuse_Shortwave_Radiation" ;
	SCA_SWdown:units = "W/m2" ;
LWdown, rlds
	LWdown:long_name = "Surface_Incident_Longwave_Radiation" ;
	LWdown:units = "W/m2" ;
PSurf, ps_fp
	PSurf:long_name = "Surface_Pressure" ;
	PSurf:units = "Pa" ;
Rainf, prrain
	Rainf:long_name = "Rainfall_Rate" ;
	Rainf:units = "Kg/m2/s" ;
Snowf, prrsnow
	Snowf:long_name = "Snowfall_Rate" ;
	Snowf:units = "Kg/m2/s" ;
CO2air
	CO2air:long_name = "Near_Surface_CO2_Concentration" ;
	CO2air:units = "Kg/m3" ;
Wind_DIR
	Wind_DIR:long_name = "Wind_Direction" ;
	Wind_DIR:units = "deg" ;

